So the answer should be 333. Let me make sure there isn't a smaller number. Since the numbers are 111, 222, 333, etc., 333 is indeed the first one that meets the divisibility rule. 

Therefore, the smallest 3-digit number of the form aaa divisible by 9 is 333.
